- Arm 3 (31b-v012, root thinking 4096) vs arm 1 (v009, thinking 0): resolved 10/33 vs 4/33, ON-only 6 / OFF-only 0, p = 0.031,
  but timeouts 21 vs 4 and empty patches 18 vs 12 -> ON-BETTER-VETOED (results/plan009_arm3_vs_arm1.json, report 021).
- Hypothesis: the 3.5-min cap is consumed by long thinking blocks; halving the root thinking budget cuts timeouts and empty diffs
  while keeping most of the resolved gain. Expected: timeouts ~10-15/33, empties <= 14/33, resolved 7-10/33.
- If v012 scores COMPLETE on Nov 8, v014 differs from v012 only by thinking 2048 <= 4096 -> finals-eligible under dec 087 (b) with
  no slot of its own (pre-check ELIGIBLE: results/finals_eligibility_31b_v014_vs_v012_precheck.json; re-run after v012 is COMPLETE).

