## Protocol (= plan 009 arm 3 verbatim except the bundle and base)
- Ids: the same 33 dev ids, fixed order eval/plans/007-arm1-ids.txt (sha256 127d32f9...e49e9), k=1, seed as arms 1-3.
- Kernel path, classifiers (GOVERNING d4cdf0f0, a208a023 alongside), IDENTITY (ZIP / CONTENT / TRANSPORT), VALIDITY (H >= 5 of 33
  literal -> INVALID), rerun rules, ENV DRIFT record, D73.7 missing-id rule, Addendum S81 stray rule and S81.5 rounding: all exactly
  as plan 009 (eval/plans/009.md), with "arm 4" for "arm 3" and BASE = arm 3 (31b-v012, rows runs/31b-v012-p9a-{smoke,main}, not re-run).
- SMOKE = first 2 ids of the registered order. PASS iff (i) each row has >= 1 root thinking block and >= 5 together;
  (ii) agent_clock_seconds <= 220 s and finalization_seconds <= 30 s per row; (iii) plan 009 mechanics + identity.
  (i) fail -> INVALID by construction, report. (ii)/(iii) fail -> no main, report.
- MAIN = ids 3..33. Smoke + main pushed in the SAME quota week (week starting 2026-11-14T00:00Z; arm 3 cost +10.33 h smoke+main,
  so ~11 h needed). Quota logged before/after smoke and main. If the week has < 12 h free when ready, the schedule goes to the Director.

## Metrics (eval/plan008_metrics.py, new `arm4` mode = arm3 mode with base dirs = arm-3 dirs; codex-reviewed CLEAN before data)
- PRIMARY: resolved discordants ARM4-only / ARM3-only, exact two-sided sign test; arm-4 resolved/33 with Wilson 95% CI.
- TIMEOUTS (plan 007 definition): arm-4 count vs arm 3 (21) and vs arm 1 (4); paired timeout discordants reported.
- EMPTY (plan 007 definition, verified_patch_bytes == 0): arm-4 count vs arm 3 (18) and arm 1 (12).
- TIMING: every row agent_clock_seconds <= 220 s, finalization_seconds <= 30 s (unrounded).
- SAFETY: test-file edits 0 rows; governing stray (S81.1) 0 rows; total wall p90 <= 1.10 x arm-3 p90; submitted-without-test <= arm 3 + 3.
- SECONDARY (descriptive, no rule): the plan-009 rule applied arm 4 vs arm 1 (ON-ADOPT / ON-BETTER-VETOED / ...), so the ship case
  against the thinking-off base is on file.
- DESCRIPTIVE: root thinking blocks/chars per task, context-overflow rows, repeat metric, LLM/tool calls p50/p90, per repo.

## Decision rule (written before any arm-4 data)
Let D = ARM3-only - ARM4-only (net resolved loss from halving thinking).
- 2048-ADOPT: D <= 2 (non-inferior within noise), AND arm-4 timeouts <= 16 (arm 3 - 5), AND arm-4 empties <= 18 (<= arm 3), AND
  TIMING and every SAFETY metric pass -> v014 replaces v012 as the 31B default draft (finals-eligible via dec 087 (b) only if v012 is
  COMPLETE and eval/finals_eligibility.py v014 vs v012 says ELIGIBLE).
- 2048-WORSE: D >= 3 -> keep v012 (thinking 4096) as the thinking-on draft; report.
- 2048-NO-GAIN: D <= 2 but the timeout or empty limit fails -> keep v012; report the timing data (no automatic further arm).
- VETOED: D <= 2 and the limits pass but TIMING or SAFETY fail -> keep v012; report.
- INVALID: smoke (i) fails, H >= 5 of 33, or the pairing is voided -> no rule applies.
- Power caveat: k=1, n=33. The non-inferiority margin of 2 is a noise allowance, not proof of equality; a 2048-ADOPT verdict says
  v014 is not detectably worse while timing out less. Timeout/empty limits are counts, not tests; paired discordants are listed.
- The finals pick between v012 / v014 / v009 is the Director's; this rule only sets the default draft.

## Later arm (not part of this pre-registration's rule): tool-level empty-patch lever on top of v012 (dec 081 item 5, dec 089 item 6)
- CPU design only now: tolerant edit_file error handling + an exploration-budget signal. It changes tools/prompt, so it is a new
  bundle that needs its OWN scored submission (dec 087) and its own addendum/pre-registration with a rule BEFORE any data.

