ops/codex/ask-20261105T181222.md:3:1. **Caps, context overflow, and patch recovery**
ops/codex/ask-20261105T181222.md:5:   Time/turn exceptions and ordinary agent exceptions—including a context-overflow exception—reach fallback collection. Tool/turn budget exits do too. Without a successful submission, the harness runs `git add -N .`, then `git diff --binary _swegemma_baseline`, falling back to `HEAD`, and strips protected files. Calling `submit_patch` is **not required**. See [agent_runner.py:932](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:932), [exception handling:1026](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1026), and [fallback:1054](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1054).
ops/codex/ask-20261105T181222.md:15:   See [fallback failure handling:1063](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1063), [cleanup:1105](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1105), and [worker error result:495](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/evaluate.py:495). Thus ordinary cap/context failures preserve existing eligible edits, but “always” is too strong.
ops/codex/ask-20261105T181222.md:52:4. **Compaction/context settings**
ops/codex/ask-20261105T181222.md:56:   Library `EvalConfig` defaults both compaction and context caching to **`None`**. Our local eval loader accepts these settings, but the timing runner reads only selected budget fields and hardcodes compaction to interval **15**, overlap **2**, threshold **14,336**, retention **5**. Adding bundle YAML keys therefore does not change that timing path. See [config.py:117](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/config.py:117), [local loader:333](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/run_agent_eval.py:333), and [timing configuration:385](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/kaggle/agent_timing.py:385).
