ops/codex/review-20261107T112341.md:17:- **Timeout and exception recovery exist, but cannot create missing edits.** The installed harness places generation inside a 210-second `asyncio.timeout`, catches ordinary model exceptions, then attempts fallback diff collection. Consequently, a context exception inside that loop does **not inherently discard an existing workspace diff in this installed version**. Recovery can still return empty when nothing changed, protected changes are stripped, collection fails, or an empty explicit submission already set `patch_submitted`. See [timeout:718](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:718), [exception/fallback path:1039](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1039), and [empty submission acceptance:111](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:111). Thinking receives no additional time allowance. Synchronous commands can delay cancellation near the deadline; their timeout has a five-second minimum floor: [execution.py:31](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:31).
